<h2>Install on 9front</h2>

<h3>Option A: install-go.rc (recommended)</h3>

<p>One-shot installer that downloads the tarball for <code>$objtype</code>,
verifies its sha256, restarts <code>webfs</code>, and extracts into
<code>$goroot</code> (default <code>/sys/lib/go</code>).</p>

<p>Fresh install (no existing <code>/sys/lib/go</code>):</p>

<pre>% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc</pre>

<p>With flags (<code>-y</code> to back up and replace an existing
install, custom <code>-goroot</code>, etc.).  9front rc has no
<code>--</code> flag-end; pipe into the dot builtin so the script sees
the positional args:</p>

<pre>% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc -c '. /fd/0 -y'
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc | rc -c '. /fd/0 -y -goroot $home/go'</pre>

<p>Or, fetch first if you want to read it before running:</p>

<pre>% hget @@BASE_URL@@/install-go.rc &gt; /tmp/install-go.rc
% rc /tmp/install-go.rc -y</pre>

<p>Available flags:</p>

<ul>
  <li><code>-base URL</code> &mdash; override the download root
      (default <code>@@BASE_URL@@</code>)</li>
  <li><code>-goroot DIR</code> &mdash; override the install location
      (default <code>/sys/lib/go</code>)</li>
  <li><code>-arch ARCH</code> &mdash; override <code>$objtype</code>
      (<code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>)</li>
  <li><code>-y</code> &mdash; non-interactive: back up any existing
      <code>$goroot</code> before installing</li>
</ul>

<h3>Option B: manual</h3>

<p>Pick the tarball matching <code>$objtype</code> (<code>amd64</code> or
<code>arm64</code>):</p>

<pre>% cd /sys/lib
% hget @@BASE_URL@@/go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz | gunzip | tar x
% bind -bc /sys/lib/go/bin /$objtype/bin
% GOROOT=/sys/lib/go go version</pre>

<h3>After install</h3>

<p>To make <code>go</code> available in every shell, add to
<code>$home/lib/profile</code>:</p>

<pre>GOROOT=/sys/lib/go
path=($path /sys/lib/go/bin)</pre>

<h2>Verify</h2>

<pre>% hget @@BASE_URL@@/SHA256SUMS &gt; /tmp/SHA256SUMS
% sha1sum -2 256 go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz
% grep go-plan9-$objtype.tar.gz /tmp/SHA256SUMS</pre>

<p>The two sha256 hex strings must match.</p>

<h2>Tarball layout</h2>

<p>Each archive expands to a single top-level <code>go/</code> directory
(upstream convention):</p>

<pre>go/
  VERSION  LICENSE  PATENTS  README.md
  api/  doc/  lib/  misc/  src/  test/
  bin/{go,gofmt}                        # plan9/$objtype binaries
  pkg/tool/plan9_$objtype/{compile,link,asm,vet,cgo,...}
  pkg/include/</pre>

<h2>Status</h2>

<ul>
  <li><b>plan9/amd64</b>: supported upstream. This build also includes the
  deadline-handling and <code>tcpsplice</code> improvements made while
  bringing up arm64.</li>
  <li><b>plan9/arm64</b>: new port. See the merge-pending
  <a href="https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/go/+/719643">Gerrit CL 719643</a>.</li>
  <li><b>9front kernel</b>: this Go release expects a 9front kernel
  containing the <code>tcpsplice</code>-close race fix
  (<code>bypeerclosed</code> field in <code>Tcpctl</code>, handled in
  <code>tcpsetstate</code> and <code>tcpclose</code>).
  A pre-patched 9front kernel source tarball can be requested separately.</li>
</ul>

